<title>USA: Nev. Mohave 790 MW unit 1 restart delayed to Wed.</title>
<headline>Nev. Mohave 790 MW unit 1 restart delayed to Wed.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Restart of the 790 megawatt (MW) unit 1 at the Mohave coal-fired power plant near Laughlin, Nev., has been delayed until Wednesday, a spokesman for Southern California Edison Co said Tuesday.</p>
<p>The unit was shut Friday due to a tube leak, which has been repaired, but some work is now being done on a generator, he said.</p>
<p>Edison is the majority owner and operator of the Mohave plant.</p>
<p>--D Beasley, Los Angeles bureau + 1 213 955 6761</p>
